From 1b0aa6dfbb869abde5cd0a7d01e808b3c8daff28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 20:05:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] v4.5: RT safety valve: fix rq->curr context bug via
 llist

Replace the broken rq->curr approach in balance_callback workers with
lockless linked lists (llist).  The previous implementation assumed
the target task was always rq->curr, which is false in enqueue_task_fair()
(the waking task is the callback target, not the currently running task).

Fix:
- Add struct llist_node demote_node and restore_node to infinity_ctx
- Per-CPU llist_head queues accumulate tasks needing demotion/restoration
- Workers drain the entire list via llist_del_all + llist_for_each_entry_safe
- llist_add's return value (true if list was empty) gates queue_balance_callback
  to avoid redundant callbacks
- container_of() links from infinity_ctx back to task_struct

This also handles the multiple-wakeup case correctly: when several demoted
tasks wake on the same tick, all are added to the llist and processed by a
single balance_callback invocation.

