Replace the over-engineered task_work/callback_head/sched_setattr cross-class
demotion with native kernel primitives:

RT safety valve: rogue SCHED_FIFO tasks exceeding 95% rt_ema are now
throttled inline in task_tick_rt() via requeue_task_rt() + resched_curr().
This keeps the task in its original scheduling class -- Plymouth retains
its SCHED_FIFO priority and is not starved by boot services.

Cgroup defense: modulation moved back to update_cfs_group() (the canonical
place for group weight computation).  The previous update_deadline()
approach fought update_cfs_group() on every tick, causing PELT thrashing.

Removed: flags, saved_rt_priority, saved_rt_policy, callback_head
demote_work/restore_work from struct infinity_ctx.  Removed all
task_work_add, sched_setattr_nocheck, init_task_work machinery.
