From 76dd27a5c6cd292c2c243e85bac805afc68bd0bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 23:15:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] v4.6-gpu: Infinity GPU scheduler extension

Implement all 4 features from PRD-001:

1. GPU Time Tracking: gpu_time_ema, gpu_time_total, gpu_time_last_active
   fields on drm_sched_entity. EMA climbs on job completion, decays on idle.
   Captures PID at entity_init via get_task_pid().

2. Virtual GPU Time: drm_sched_entity_calc_vtime() replaces submit
   timestamp with normalized vtime scaled by priority and EMA burstiness.
   min_gpu_vtime on drm_sched_rq prevents catch-up starvation trap.
   DRM_SCHED_POLICY_INFINITY selects the scheduler.

3. Soft Priority: KERNEL priority is always serviced first via standalone
   FIFO. HIGH/NORMAL/LOW get proportional share via vtime scaling factors
   (no strict starvation).

4. Cross-Scheduler Coupling: entity->last_user_pid resolves to task_struct
   under RCU read lock. futex_waiting halves vtime, EMA=0 halves vtime
   again -- interactive CPU tasks get GPU priority.

Backward compatible: oldest_job_waiting (ktime_t) is preserved untouched.
Switching sched_policy=0 restores stock FIFO behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
